---
/** English twin of /suppression-de-compte — see that file for why this page exists. */
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
const turnstileSiteKey = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY;
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Delete an account or a profile"
  description="How to delete an adult account or a learner's profile in the Bitaqat Hifd Qor'an app, from the app or by request."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-600">Application</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900 dark:text-white">
      Delete an account or a profile
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
      The <strong>Bitaqat Hifd Qor'an</strong> app (<span class="font-mono text-sm">com.bitaqat.hifdquran</span>)
      lets you delete everything from within the app itself. This page is for those who no longer
      can — app uninstalled, phone lost, device out of service.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6">
      <a
        href="#request"
        class="inline-block rounded-full bg-ink-900 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-gold-600 dark:bg-white dark:text-ink-900 dark:hover:bg-gold-400"
      >
        Request a deletion
      </a>
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-night-300">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">From the app, right away</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">This is the fastest path, and it needs nobody's approval.</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 ps-6">
          <li>
            <strong>You are an adult</strong> (parent, guardian or teacher): <em>Guardian</em> or
            <em>Mentor</em> tab → <em>Settings</em> → <em>Delete my account</em>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>You are the learner</strong>, on your own device: <em>Settings</em> →
            <em>Delete my profile</em>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>You are a minor's guardian</strong>: open the child's page →
            <em>Delete this child's profile</em>. The gesture asks for your password and the child's
            travel name. A teacher can never do it: that right belongs to the adult who consented for
            the child.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div id="what-goes">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">What is deleted, and what stays</h2>

        <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">A learner's profile</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The profile first goes into a <strong>30-day bin</strong>: it becomes invisible everywhere in
          the app and nothing circulates for it any more, but its guardian can still bring it back. On
          the 31st day everything is erased, with no way back: travel name, avatar, progress,
          validation requests, evaluations received, deadlines, badges, rewards, sessions, history and
          notifications — along with the device's anonymous session.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Before deleting, the app offers to <strong>save a copy</strong> of the journey, handed over on
          the device. That file is not sent anywhere.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">An adult account</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Deleted: the account itself, its email address, its display name, its preferences, its
          invitation codes and the notification tokens of its devices.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <strong>Not</strong> deleted: the profiles of the learners it followed. An adult neither owns
          nor holds a learner — they are that learner's teacher or guardian. Those profiles go back to
          “waiting for a teacher”, and the evaluations the adult had given stay in the learner's
          history, without an author's name. A child does not lose their work because an adult leaves.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-5 font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">Backups</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">
          An encrypted copy of the database is made every night and kept for 14 days, then
          destroyed. It is never used to restore a deleted account.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">What the app does not hold</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          There is nothing to delete of what was never collected. The app asks for no date of birth, no
          legal name, no phone number, no postal address. It measures no duration, reaches neither
          microphone, nor camera, nor location, and contains no tracker and no advertising. A learner
          has no email address: their device signs in anonymously. Data is hosted in the European
          Union.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div id="request" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink-900 dark:text-white">Make a request</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you no longer have access to the app, write to us here. Give the email address of the
          adult account concerned and — if a child is involved — the travel name they used in the app.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Every request is <strong>verified and then handled by hand</strong>: we reply to the address
          you give before anything is deleted. That is slower than a button, and deliberately so — a
          public form must not be able to erase a child's journey on the strength of a typed address
          alone. Allow a few days.
        </p>

        <form
          id="contact-form"
          class="mt-8 space-y-5"
          data-objet="suppression"
          data-msg-missing-turnstile="Please complete the security check before sending."
          data-msg-sending="Sending…"
          data-msg-success="Request sent. We will reply to this address before anything is deleted."
          data-msg-error="Something went wrong. Please try again in a moment."
        >
          <div>
            <label for="name" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink-700 dark:text-night-200">Name</label>
            <input
              type="text"
              id="name"
              name="name"
              required
              maxlength="100"
              class="mt-1 w-full rounded-lg border border-ink-200 bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-sm text-ink-900 focus:border-gold-400 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-gold-400 dark:border-night-700 dark:bg-night-900 dark:text-white"
            />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink-700 dark:text-night-200">
              Email of the account to delete
            </label>
            <input
              type="email"
              id="email"
              name="email"
              required
              maxlength="200"
              class="mt-1 w-full rounded-lg border border-ink-200 bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-sm text-ink-900 focus:border-gold-400 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-gold-400 dark:border-night-700 dark:bg-night-900 dark:text-white"
            />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="message" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink-700 dark:text-night-200">
              What should be deleted
            </label>
            <textarea
              id="message"
              name="message"
              required
              maxlength="5000"
              rows="6"
              placeholder="The adult account, a child's profile (give their travel name), or both."
              class="mt-1 w-full rounded-lg border border-ink-200 bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-sm text-ink-900 focus:border-gold-400 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-gold-400 dark:border-night-700 dark:bg-night-900 dark:text-white"
            ></textarea>
          </div>

          <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={turnstileSiteKey}></div>

          <button
            type="submit"
            id="contact-submit"
            class="w-full rounded-full bg-gold-500 px-7 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-gold-500/20 transition-colors hover:bg-gold-600 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-60"
          >
            Send the request
          </button>
          <p id="contact-status" role="status" class="text-center text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-night-400"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>
  <script src="/scripts/contact.js" defer></script>
</Layout>
